Clocks set to box local time by G0, so device and host stamps are comparable.

## Why port1.0.48 is the binding point
`access-group` is an INGRESS filter. Host->swi_b traffic ingresses the DUT on port1.0.48, so a
rule written src=host dst=swi_b matches directly there. (Contrast T44992, where the ACL was on
the aggregator `sa1` and the matching flow was the RETURN direction.)

## Tools
cfg.py, ckcon.py, ckyn.py, ckreload.py from tools/, copied to tb277:/tmp/ck-g23-acl-2026-10-09.

