host# ping .70 from 10.38.22.66 ->   0% packet loss           STILL PERMITTED
x960-56YSQ#show platform classifier statistics utilization brief
  Loop Detection      2
  ACL                 1
  Total               3 / 1024 (0.29%)
  => STEP 7 PASS: the ACL definitions, the port binding and the enforcement all survived a
     save and reload.
     FINDING: six lists are defined but only ONE is bound, and the classifier reports ACL 1.
     An UNBOUND access-list consumes NO TCAM. The Falcon rule budget is spent by BINDINGS,
     not by definitions -- which matters directly to the Test Strategy's named risk, because
     a configuration can hold far more rules than the pool if most are unbound.

## Findings
F1  A numbered hardware ACL CANNOT BE EDITED while an `access-group` binds it:
    `% This access-list is currently attached to an interface so cannot be edited.` The entry
    is silently not added -- `show access-list` must be re-read to notice. Unbind first, or
    use one list per rule.
    Contrast the NAMED sub-mode, where `% This access-list is attached to an interface...` is
    an ADVISORY and the edit applies on `end`. One word apart, opposite meanings.
F2  `deny proto 1` is stored and displayed as `deny icmp`. The CLI canonicalises a protocol
    number to its named form.
F3  An UNBOUND access-list consumes no classifier entry; TCAM is spent per BINDING.
F4  A port accepts multiple `access-group` lines simultaneously (five were bound at once).

VERDICT: PASS -- numbered hardware IP ACLs in the 3000-3699 range bind to a port with
`access-group`, and deny and permit both work across all five protocol forms (icmp, ip,
proto, tcp, udp) with correct protocol selectivity -- TCP and UDP rules leave ICMP alone while
icmp, ip and proto 1 rules deny it. Non-matching sources are unaffected, ARP is unaffected,
permit rules are proven by an advancing counter rather than by the implicit permit, each bound
rule costs exactly one of the 1024 classifier entries, and the configuration and its
enforcement survive a reload. One platform constraint the case text does not anticipate was
found and is recorded: a bound numbered list cannot be edited.
